{
  "id": "gateways",
  "title": "Calling a method in another language",
  "summary": "`@Gateway` declares a method that code in another language answers. The target is a class in another Yon language, such as `server/services/ReportService.java`. It can also be a program, such as `python3 server/helpers/forecast.py`. The arguments are sent as JSON, within fixed limits. The answer becomes the result of the method. A failure becomes a `BehaviorError` with a fixed message. The build checks every target. Only one hop (one call from one language to another) is allowed. In the example, JavaScript and TypeScript call the Java class `ReportService.java`, and Python calls it too. Java, Groovy and every other language call the Python class `LedgerService.py`, and every language also runs the program `forecast.py`. Lua cannot declare a gateway yet: the build refuses `@Gateway` in Lua with `TY1308`. C++ has no tab here, because C++ Yon code has only route controllers so far: the build refuses `Service` in C++ with `TY1308` (ADR 0099).",
